adjudication.rationale:
In `checkIfIsAvailable` (added in this diff), the working-hours bounds check computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
```
This makes `end` a copy of the start time instead of using the slot’s end (e.g., `slotEndTime`), so a slot that starts within working hours but ends after `workingHour.endTime` will not be rejected. That matches the finding and is a correctness defect visible in the diff.

In `checkIfIsAvailable`, the new working-hours validation computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
```
So `end` always equals `start` (copy-paste error) and never reflects `slotEndTime`. This makes the `end > workingHour.endTime` check ineffective for slots that start within working hours but extend past the end, allowing such slots to be incorrectly treated as within working hours.
